<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#0A1020', fontFamily: 'Arial', padding: '52px 60px 30px 60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#4D8DFF', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2.2 }}>02 · QUANTITIES</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 36, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.2, marginTop: 8 }}>
        Two symbols carry the whole argument
    </Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 1160, height: 1, background: '#24334C', marginTop: 14 }} />

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 24, marginTop: 20 }}>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '18px 22px', background: '#111B2E', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 20, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Λ — what the chain arm recovers</Text>
            <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', marginTop: 2, height: 84 }}>
                <Math latex='\Lambda \;=\; \frac{R^{2}_{\mathrm{chain}} - R^{2}_{\mathrm{unit}}}{1 - R^{2}_{\mathrm{unit}}}' width={280} color='#FFFFFF' />
            </Box>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.5, marginTop: 8 }}>
                <span style={{ color: '#FFB020', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>Not clipped.</span> A negative Λ is a result — the chain arm did worse on the same test rows.
            </Text>
        </Box>

        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '18px 22px', background: '#111B2E', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 6 }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 20, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>Slope κ — how fast Λ moves with data</Text>
            <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', marginTop: 2, height: 84 }}>
                <Math latex='\kappa \;=\; \frac{d\Lambda}{d\,\log_{10} n}' width={210} color='#FFFFFF' />
            </Box>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.5, marginTop: 8 }}>
                <span style={{ color: '#FFB020', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>Not pooled OLS.</span> Slope per fold, then averaged — one wide fold cannot decide the slope.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 24, marginTop: 16 }}>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '14px 20px', background: '#16233A', borderLeft: '2px solid #4D8DFF' }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 19, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>n — training rows, never total rows</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.45, marginTop: 6 }}>
                Levels 300 / 1,000 / 3,000 / 10,000 / all 22,242. Test rows are identical at every level; only the training prefix shrinks.
            </Text>
        </Box>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', padding: '14px 20px', background: '#16233A', borderLeft: '2px solid #4D8DFF' }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 19, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>n* — where the two arms cross</Text>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#C3D0E2', lineHeight: 1.45, marginTop: 6 }}>
                The row count at which ΔR² changes sign. Descriptive, no interval; reported only where the sign changes inside the window.
            </Text>
        </Box>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ marginTop: 'auto', padding: '10px 16px', background: '#0E1728', border: '1px solid #24334C', borderRadius: 4 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#A8B8CE', lineHeight: 1.45 }}>
            Also fixed here: ΔR² ≡ R²_chain − R²_unit, the numerator of Λ · ρ = Spearman correlation between Λ and tier (H1) ·
            dex = a log10 ratio, so 1 dex is a tenfold change. Rules applied throughout: a slope is reported only where the window spans ≥ 0.5 dex, and a cell is left empty where 1 − R²_unit &lt; 0.05.
        </Text>
    </Box>

    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', marginTop: 10 }}>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>Group 32 · How Much Is a Chain Worth?</Text>
        <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8FA3BC' }}>3 / 18</Text>
    </Box>
</Slide>
